        "passageTitle": "Wonder Ridge Radio Broadcast Schedule, Monday-Friday",
        "passageText": "=== Văn bản 1 ===\nWonder Ridge Radio Broadcast Schedule, Monday-Friday\n\n6A.M.-Noon | Noon-4 P.M. | 4 P.M.-7 P.M. | 7 P.M.10 P.M.\n\nCOFFEEBREAK | AFTERNOONJAZZ | FOLKFRENZY | JOSIE'SJOINT\n\nLocal news and | Music from | Folk music | Modern sounds\n\ninterviews with | traditional jazz | from around | selected by our\n\ncommunity | to jazzfusion | the world | station's own\n\nmembers | music director\n\nHost: | Host: | Host: | Host:\n\nFelice Finney | Malachi Mzee | Penny Ariza | Josie Jones\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\n*E-mail*\n\nTo: | feedback@wonderridgeradio.org From: | pfabre@sendmail.net Subject: | My new radio station!\n\nDate: | October 22\n\nTothefolksat Wonder Ridge Radio: As I was driving last week, I got tired of listening to sports talk and turned the dial. Suddenly, my car was filled with a song that I hadn't heard in many years. It was traditional music from France, where my grandmother was born. She used to play that song when I was a child. I never expected to hear it on the radio here in Wonder Ridge. Thanks for this experience and for all your great programs. Your new fan, Pierre Fabre\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\nWonder Ridge Radio Job Opening:Programming Assistant Posted November 2 Job Description The programming assistant reports to the director of programming and supports the radio station by performing a variety of research and communication functions. This role is an entry-level, part-time position. Responsibilities Conducting background research on interviewees Keeping up-to-date on news and news makers in order to suggest potential topics and guests for on-air interviews Updating the station's Web site and program host biography pages Using scheduling software to update the broadcast schedule Communicating with listeners, especially via e-mail and social media To apply, e-mail a resume and cover letter to hiring@wonderridgeradio.org.",
